    "lawCode": "Amd §57-0107, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6357\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to the Central Pine Barrens area and the core preservation area\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo protect the Long Island Pine Barrens.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would make technical amendments to the metes and bounds of the\nLong Island Pine Barrens.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Long Island Central Pine Barrens is one of the few Pine Barrens in\nthe world. Home to thousands of plants and animal species, its unique\nbiodiversity is more extensive than anywhere in the State and depends on\nthe survival of this ecosystem to thrive. The Long Island Central Pine\nBarrens also supplies drinking water for much of Long Island through its\naquifers, the first in the nation to be designated a Sole Source Aquifer\nby the EPA. Incorporating this unprotected part of the Pine Barrens in\nShoreham into the State's Pine Barrens boundaries would ensure that this\nnatural treasure survives.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
